# The asset names of a hostkeeper release, one per line, `<version>` standing for X.Y.Z: the
# contract that cargo xtask release (crates/xtask/src/release/contract.rs, asset_names) keeps.
# A name may be added (add it here in the same pull request); a name is never removed or
# renamed, since consumers fetch assets by these names, unless it is withdrawn: a line
# `withdrawn: <name>` is a name a release once held and no longer does, each listed with its reason
# in crates/xtask/src/release/contract/tests.rs (WITHDRAWN). Lines starting with `#` are comments.
# `hello_<version>_<arch>.deb`, `hello-<version>-macos-arm64.pkg` and `mdm_<version>_amd64.deb` are
# the services' native packages (docs/design/packages-native.md, item A21); hello's failing build
# has its `.deb`s alone, `hello_<version>-fail-ready_<arch>.deb` (section 10.10). The archive packages
# (`*.tar.zst`, their `.sha256` and bundles) and the release indexes (`index.json`,
# `hello-index.json`, `hello-fail-ready-index.json`, `mdm-index.json`) are withdrawn
# (docs/design/packages-native.md, item A28).
